   "text": {
    "L1": "A remainder is not an automatic instruction. The story tells us what to do.",
    "L2": "Here is a myth: always drop the remainder. That is wrong when people still need a group.",
    "L3": "In the worked example, 52 divided by 5 is 10 remainder 2.",
    "L4": "Ten cars carry 50 people. Two people are still left, so one more car is needed.",
    "L5": "When everyone must fit, round up to the next group.",
    "L6": "When only full groups count, drop the remainder. If the question asks what is left, give the remainder.",
    "L7": "Always read the question again after dividing. The same division can give different answers in different stories.",
    "L8": "Now choose the number of autos needed for 23 students, with 4 students in each auto."
   },
